## 4. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths` accepts a shard number with leading zeros inconsistently and rewrites only 5 digits

**Responsibility.** Resolve any shard path to the full ordered shard list.

**Problem.** The check `any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5` hard-codes `.gguf` as exactly 5 characters and the total as exactly 5 digits; a model named `...-00001-of-00010.gguf` works, but the function silently returns `{any}` (single-shard) for a 6-digit total (`-of-000010`), which is a *different* model family and should be an error, not a silent single-shard read. Also `no > n` returns `{any}` instead of throwing, so a corrupt name `...-00007-of-00005.gguf` is treated as a one-shard model and later fails with a confusing "duplicate tensor" or missing-tensor error.

**Change.** Distinguish "not a split name" from "a malformed split name".

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@
     int no = 0, n = 0;
     for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
         const char a = any[at - 5 + i], b = any[at + 4 + i];
-        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {any};
+        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {any};   // not a split name at all
         no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
         n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
     }
-    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
+    // A well-formed -NNNNN-of-MMMMM suffix whose numbers are impossible (no > n, n == 0)
+    // is a corrupt name, not a single-shard model: refuse rather than mis-open one shard.
+    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n)
+        throw std::runtime_error("malformed split shard name " + any + " (shard " + std::to_string(no) +
+                                 " of " + std::to_string(n) + ")");
```

**Verification.**
1. `gguf_split_test`: a path `model-00007-of-00005.gguf` now throws with that message instead of returning one path.
2. A non-split path `model.gguf` and a 6-digit-total path still return `{any}` (the digit loop rejects them before the new throw).

