## 7. `include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp` — `conversation_mem_available` is declared but not defined in the header and has no parsing contract

**Responsibility.** Host physical-memory telemetry for the parking admission policy.

**Problem.** The header declares `conversation_mem_available(std::istream&)` but the supplied excerpt gives no implementation contract; the `.cpp` is not shown. The inline `conversation_memory_admit` treats `std::nullopt` as "refuse", which is correct, but `conversation_available_memory()` returning `nullopt` on Linux when `/proc/meminfo` is unreadable silently disables parking with no diagnostic.

**Change.** Document the contract in the header and add a reason out-parameter so the engine can log why parking is off.

